<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Combat</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>kill &lt;character&gt;
hit &lt;character&gt;
</pre>
<p>kill or hit starts a fight. You strike with the weapon you wield, or your 
bare hands, round after round, until one of you falls, dies or flees. While 
you fight you can give other orders too: cast spells, use your skills, 
rescue a friend.
</p><p>Before you start, <a cmd='#'>consider</a> your foe to see how strong it is. During the 
fight, <a cmd='#'>diagnose</a> shows how badly hurt it is. If the fight goes against 
you, <a cmd='#'>flee</a>; wimpy mode makes you flee by yourself when you are badly hurt 
(see <a cmd='#'>Help Wimpy Mode</a>).
</p><p>When someone falls stunned, incapacitated or mortally wounded, the fight 
stops: to finish them off, you must attack again.
</p><p>You can only fight other players if both of you have signed the Book of 
Blood (see <a cmd='#'>Help BoB</a>).
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Kill</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Consider</a>
